# TFG VISTA3D Medical Imaging

Prototype project for 3D medical image segmentation and quantitative reporting.

The project focuses on kidney/tumor/cyst segmentation, volumetric analysis, evaluation metrics and structured report generation from medical imaging masks.

## Main goals

- Organize the medical imaging workflow as a reproducible Python project.
- Run segmentation experiments using MONAI/VISTA3D-style tools.
- Compute volumes, Dice/Jaccard metrics, connected components and anatomical summaries.
- Generate structured JSON reports and human-readable summaries.
- Keep notebooks for demonstrations, while maintaining reusable code in src/.

## Project structure

- src/vista3d_tfg/: reusable Python package.
- 
otebooks/: exploration and demo notebooks.
- data/: local datasets, ignored by Git.
- outputs/: generated tables, figures and reports, ignored by Git.
- docs/: methodology and result notes.
- 	ests/: basic reproducibility tests.

## Environment

Recommended environment:

`ash
conda create -n vista3d-tfg-311 python=3.11
conda activate vista3d-tfg-311


